141 - What Child Is This?
 / 
Key: G
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 141
Topic: Jesus Christ - 

Verse 1:
[C/G]What child [Em/B]is [G]this, who, laid to rest, [D]On Mary's lap is sleeping?
[Em]Whom angels greet [Bm]with anthems [G/B]sweet, While shepherds [D/F#]watch are keeping?
[F#dim]This, this is [Bm/F#]Christ the King, [Am]Whom shepherds [D]guard and angels sing:
[D]Haste, haste to bring Him [G]laud, [Em]The babe, the son [Bm]of Mary.

Refrain:
[D]This, this is Christ the King,
[D]Whom shepherds guard and angels [G]sing:
[F#dim]Haste, haste [Bm/F#]to bring [Am]Him laud,
[C/G]The babe, the son of Mary.

Verse 2:
[C/G]Why [Em/B]lies [G]He in [D]such mean estate
[Em]Where ox [Bm]and [G/B]ass are [D/F#]feeding?
[F#dim]Good Christian, [Bm/F#]fear: [Am]for [D]sinners here
[D]The silent [G]Word [Em]is pleading.

Verse 3:
[C/G]So [Em/B]bring [G]Him incense, [D/F#]gold, and myrrh,
[Em]Come, peasant, [G/B]king, to [D/F#]own Him,
[F#dim]The King [Bm/F#]of kings [Am]salvation [D]brings,
[D]Let loving [G]hearts [Em]enthrone [Bm]Him.
